INT. ABANDONED CARNIVAL - HALL OF MIRRORS - NIGHT

Cracked glass multiplies everything. A hundred reflections of a hundred flashlights, swimming in the dark.

Four silhouettes pick through the maze. DETECTIVE NAOMI FAIRWEATHER (40s, rain jacket, gun at her hip). Her partner DETECTIVE CASPIAN ROTH (30s, tall, careful). A hostage, LUCIA FERREIRA (20s, torn dress, hands bound), shoved ahead by the fourth: THE CARNY (50s, grease-stained vest, a pistol, a nervous laugh).

THE CARNY
Don't come closer.

NAOMI
We're not.

The mirrors show otherwise. Dozens of Naomis advancing. The Carny spins, firing at a reflection. Glass explodes in a silver storm.

Lucia drops to the floor. Caspian dives behind a panel. Naomi flattens against the wall. The Carny turns, turns again, lost among his own faces.

NAOMI (CONT'D)
(low)
Caspian. Left.

He crawls. The Carny fires again. Another mirror blows. Fragments rain down on Lucia, who covers her head.

CASPIAN
(whispering)
Lucia. Stay low.

The Carny laughs, high and thin. Footsteps. A hundred of them.
